      "message": "[warning] Line 1312: 🟡 `PresenceManager::notifyDeviceListeners()` copies callbacks before invoking them, so removing this listener does not prevent an already-copied callback from running. If `stopTracking()` and a later `startTracking()` occur while an old offline callback is in flight, this callback can act on the newly initialized `trackedMembers_` and erase a currently valid device, preventing retries until another presence transition. Associate callbacks with a tracking generation/token and ignore events from older tracking sessions (or synchronize listener teardown with in-flight callbacks).",
